  "ownershipReview": [
    "Sema owns the exact Wait operand. RuntimePlan retains the same payload in global and instance facts, rejecting missing, duplicate, unrelated and non-Duration operands. One scoped query supplies the existing Flow value continuation; no fabricated callsite or reconstructed operand.",
    "Core owns typed Duration conversion and the pure positive remaining-time primitive. Counted Source codec and body metadata use the existing version1 owners and visitors. Type admission precedes child lowering; AOT excludes evaluated Wait from scalar fusion.",
    "AWBC owns one explicit Duration-source payload: Input or Constant for static packets without a register context. Codec, Serde, verifier, Product mapping and RuntimePlan producer share that choice. No empty-argument fallback, fake zero-duration host descriptor, Dynamic signature or legacy reader.",
    "Syntax gives Thread/Flow/line-plan item emission its own Flow grammar context before classifying and emitting nested statement bodies. The enclosing declaration context and obsolete indented cancellation-body parameter are removed from that path; ordinary function calls retain their selected-call grammar."
  ]
